## 5. Where this ticket's changes live

| Change | Procedure | What |
|---|---|---|
| Gap 1 — catch-up window (**REVERTED 11/12 per PO**) | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew` | `#tbl_DLQ_Installment_Research` population is back to `= @StartDays` exact match; the `BETWEEN @StartDays AND @EndDays` window was live 11/06-11/12, then reverted — an installment missed on exactly day 20 is skipped forever again, same as pre-ticket |
| Gap 2 — tax-year validation | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew` | Eligibility `EXISTS` check: added `TEMP.CurrentTaxYear = ap.CURRENT_TAX_YEAR` — still active, unaffected by the Gap 1 reversal |
| Non-determinism fix (found during testing) | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew` | `@DIRTaxYear`/`@DIRInstallmentNo`/`@DIRDueDate` pull: same year-scoping added, so it can't grab a different year's row than the eligibility check just validated |
| Dedup guard installment-blindness fix (found during testing) | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` | Guard's matching `SELECT`: added `TaxYear`/`InstallmentNo` to the business key (previously only Loan+Agency+TaxID+PropertyID+LienSEQ+SystemCode) |
| DIR carve-out | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` | New block inside the guard's `IF @WinnerExceptionID IS NOT NULL`: updates `InstallmentDueDate` in place instead of suppressing, for both open AND completed records. `SLADueDate` and the parent table's `InsertedDate` stay frozen once complete; `Tax_Info.Updatedate`/`UpdatedBy` and the audit history log always fire regardless of completion status |

